\import{fnip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fnip}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{Center manifold}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{Let #{x_{*}} be an \vocabk{equilibrium}{fnip-0014} of
#{\dot x=f(x)}, and let #{Df(x_{*})} be its
\vocabk{Jacobian}{fnip-0034}. The \newvocab{center eigenspace} is
the generalized eigenspace of #{Df(x_{*})} belonging to the
eigenvalues of real part #{0}. A \newvocab{center manifold} of
#{x_{*}} is a manifold through #{x_{*}}, tangent to the
\vocab{center eigenspace}, and locally invariant: some neighborhood
of #{x_{*}} in the manifold is carried into the manifold by the
flow for a short time in both directions.}

\p{\citet{Theorem 3.2.1, §3.2, p. 127}{guckenheimer1983nonlinear}
uses this tangency and this invariance for the manifold it denotes
#{W^{c}}. \citet{Definition 5.1, §5.1.1, p. 158}{kuznetsov2004elements}
gives the name \vocab{center manifold} to the manifold in his Theorem 5.1.}
